    <string name="notifications_note">Yew Harness notifies this phone when something needs you (a permission, a question, a decision or a held letter), when a session stops with an error, and when a task finishes. Notifications come through the encrypted channel; the relay cannot read them.</string>
    <string name="background_note">Yew Harness does not use a push service. With notifications on, the app keeps one connection to the relay while Yew Harness is open, also when it is not on screen, and Android shows a standing notification for it. When you close Yew Harness (swipe it away from recent apps) the connection ends, and notifications arrive again once you open Yew Harness; what was waiting then shows in Approvals. Turn on \"Keep receiving after Yew Harness is closed\" to keep the connection after that too, and after the phone starts or Yew Harness is updated: notifications then arrive without opening Yew Harness, and the standing notification stays. Either way the system may stop Yew Harness to save power; to make that less likely, allow Yew Harness to run without battery optimization, and on some phones allow auto-start and background running for Yew Harness in their own settings.</string>
